# fix(tests): finish worktree-safety for the test orchestrator

## Summary

Follow-up to the recent work that made `Tests.ps1` portable and
worktree-safe. While verifying every test variation from
`AGENTS.TESTING.md` inside a worktree (repo folder named `tests`, not the
module), the `ExplicitModuleImport` check was the one remaining piece that
still assumed the repo folder matched the module name. This PR fixes that
and widens the `-SignInLog` audit-log test window.

## What changed

**Worktree-safe module-name resolution in ExplicitModuleImport**

`Test-ExplicitModuleImport.ps1` resolved the module-under-test name with
`Find-ModuleRoot`, which walks up the tree looking for a `<folder>.psd1`
whose name matches its directory. In a worktree the repo folder is named
after the branch, so no matching manifest is ever found:
`Find-ModuleRoot` returns `$null` and `.Name` throws, taking the whole
check down before it scans a single file.

The orchestrator already resolves the module name from the manifest (the
worktree-safe approach used everywhere else in `Tests.ps1`). It now
exports that as `$Global:Dev_ModuleName`, and the check prefers it,
falling back to `Find-ModuleRoot` for standalone runs and erroring
clearly when neither yields a name.

**Wider SignInLog audit-log query**

The `-SignInLog` parameter-path test queried only the last 7 days of the
unified audit log; the window is now 30 days, with the context name and
header comment updated to match.

## Testing

All `Tests.ps1` variations were run in the worktree:

- `Offline` — 246 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped.
- `Online` / `Online -InteractiveAuth` — Connect-IRT passes and the silent
  cache round-trip is verified; the orchestrator loads the module from the
  manifest name, confirming worktree portability.
- `AutoFormat`, `ModuleSyntax`, `ExplicitModuleImport`, `FormatOperator`,
  `JoinPath`, `NonASCIICharacters`, `FindUnwantedStrings`,
  `WriteVerboseDebug`, `LineLength`, `BacktickContinuation`, `PSSA` — all
  clean. `ExplicitModuleImport` now passes (155 files) where it previously
  threw.
- `-Path` targeting (`LineLength -Path .\Source\Public`) scopes correctly.

## Known issue (not addressed here)

The `-SignInLog` UAL test still fails in the test tenant even at 30 days:
that tenant produces no `UserLoggedIn`/`UserLoggedOff`/`UserLoginFailed`
UAL operations (modern Entra sign-ins land in the Entra sign-in logs).
Every other UAL parameter-path assertion passes, so this is a test-tenant
data characteristic rather than a code regression. Left for a follow-up
decision (skip-on-empty vs. generating the data).
